    "moment": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "His series of twelve lithographs entitled Elles boldly confronted the reality of late 19th-century Parisian brothels on the rue de Moulins and the rue de Richelieu, in which rich men's pursuit of pleasure with the daughters of the poor was legal and accepted.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Cleveland Museum of Art",
          "title": "Elles: Woman In a Corset",
